the spinel crord, causing paralysis from the arms downwards. There was also glight conruesinn of the heals. The can was a hopeless one from the first, owing to the serious injury of the gpine.—µy the Coroner Tonal] wne not able to glee a very clear account .stn how lie fell. Be did not blame annivoly. Misn thelenn, nistren at the Cottage Floop".41, said when YoZeg wan admitled she spike to hint about the aecident, and he told her that he had fallen on his neck. He did nnt attach any blame to anybody.' Ile died at 3.25 on Wedneaday afternoon, and was unconscious for about twn hours before death. The jury returned a verdict of Accidental death," and the Coroner remerked that they all aympethiged very deeply with tho relatives in their sad bereavement.</p>
